Short:        CPU benchmarks for Amiga compilers
Author:       Bernie Innocenti <bernie@codewiz.org>
Uploader:     Bernie Innocenti <bernie@codewiz.org>
Type:         util/moni
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 2.0.4
Requires:     5 MB of free RAM, 64 KiB stack, 68040 and FPU for benchwork-040
Distribution: Aminet
Kurz:         CPU-Benchmarks fuer Amiga-Compiler

Benchwork is a set of CPU benchmarks for comparing m68k compilers, built
from code that Amiga programs actually run: LHa, zlib, libpng, the FreeType
rasterizer, Dhrystone, a dithered landscape renderer, a triangle setup loop
from a Wipeout port, the vertex projection and polygon clipper of an NFS3
port, AmiSSL's SHA-512 and AES-GCM, and memcpy/memmove patterns.
Everything works on memory buffers, so the timed region contains only
compiler-generated code: no disk, display or OS calls.

Project's home and documentation: https://github.com/codewiz/benchwork
Source of this release: https://github.com/codewiz/benchwork/tree/v@VERSION@


Binaries
--------

  benchwork-000   68000, soft float
  benchwork-020   68020, soft float
  benchwork-040   68040 with FPU

All three are built with m68k-amigaos-gcc 16.2 at -O2.


